id: pm-github-ci-v2
title: Apply Fleet CI v2 quick PR and deep validation tiers
description: Companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Replace four exhaustive PR gates with preserved required quick checks and a full post-merge matrix; retain all existing contracts and unchanged coverage thresholds. Existing runner-held sync and packed-install issues have distinct scopes.
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,"gh:unbraind/pm-github#249",performance
created_at: "2026-11-15T05:41:47.478Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T14:34:26.845Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[27]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T05:41:51.913Z",codex-sol,"Plan: preserve required test (22) and test (26), move exhaustive npm/Bun gates and native Bun suite to deep CI, retain strict tracker health and all release gate checks. CodeQL is not required. Release and reusable pm-github workflows are excluded from this task. Baseline successful main CI run 43646546806 took 1h29m25s. Related existing items: pm-github-r14n and pm-github-gaq8 remain independent fixture issues."
  "2026-11-15T05:46:17.564Z",codex-sol,"Implementation: PR tier keeps exact required names, hosted Ubuntu, 30-minute bounds, PR cancellation, and a docs/tracker cheap path. Deep retains four Node22/26 x npm/Bun gates plus both exhaustive native Bun suites, with full depth, scale 3, 120-minute bounds and 02:11 UTC schedule. Typecheck, lint and strict unique-key YAML parsing pass. Actionlint is unavailable. Baseline Node26 gate took 27m14s plus 28m34s native Bun; largest seeded models took 50.07s and 49.29s. Focused quick tests are running; an initial test-compilation typing issue was corrected."
  "2026-11-15T05:48:52.279Z",codex-sol,"PR #249 opened at implementation head 3b13dd9. New workflow detector regression passes eight Git-history cases, including docs-only, code, lockfile, workflow, newline filenames, deletion, source-to-docs rename and manual dispatch. Privacy gate passed 9542 Git objects with approved identities and no secret or host-path matches. Required PR checks are queued. Linked test result persistence is disabled by project policy, so result receipts are recorded in comments."
  "2026-11-15T06:01:37.515Z",codex-sol,"Hosted quick checks reached almost 15 minutes including less than two minutes of queue, so fixture execution remains a bottleneck beyond seeded model depth. Prepared an explicit four-worker quick-only override to overlap CLI fixture IO; default/local and every full-depth coverage invocation stay capped at two. The same complete test glob and all-source 100-percent gate remain. Fourteen focused coverage-boundary and change-detector tests pass, including full-depth rejection of the override and invalid override controls."
  "2026-11-15T06:03:20.715Z",codex-sol,"Run 43682533633 on 3b13dd9 was superseded at the 15-minute wall target, with both required checks still testing; it is cancelled evidence, not a pass. Its partial Node26 log had 581 completed tests and no assertion failure. New head dae0d49 starts run 43683592891 with effectively no queue (jobs created 06:02:12 UTC; starts 06:02:13/14). Four-worker quick CI and unchanged two-worker full/default behavior are now under hosted validation."
  "2026-11-15T06:06:41.386Z",codex-sol,"The broad changed-file local command hit its 1200-second harness cap on the shared host; this is not passing evidence. It did not complete, so a local whole-suite coverage run would not fit the requested approximately 20-minute budget and is deferred to the PR's quick coverage gate. Running focused name selections covering every edited seeded corpus and latency assertion, at quick depth and time scale 3, with the same changed-file scope. No full-depth local run has been made."
  "2026-11-15T06:09:27.831Z",codex-sol,"Further baseline/partial-log analysis found the remaining serial property corpus: 186 generated closeout decision cells (36 selection/peer combinations plus 150 claim-kind/evidence combinations) run in one file. The original literal-count search missed this Cartesian product. Quick now takes the same first 25 cells via testDepth; full/default keeps all 186 and every oracle/publication assertion. This targets a measured serial bottleneck rather than omitting a gate. Coverage thresholds and source scope remain unchanged. Local focused seeded/latency proof is still running."
  "2026-11-15T06:10:06.465Z",codex-sol,"Focused edited-test proof passed: 34 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todos, quick depth and time scale 3, using the linked exact command. Coverage boundary/detector proof passed 14 tests separately. Baseline Node26 closeout decision matrix measured 392.03 seconds for all 186 cells versus 64.65 seconds for its first 25; this supports applying the depth helper to that generated corpus. Running those 25 real end-to-end cells locally now."
  "2026-11-15T06:13:13.123Z",codex-sol,"Quick closeout matrix proof passed 25/25 real end-to-end cells in 144.970 seconds, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todos, at PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick and PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3. Typecheck, test compilation and lint pass on the current source. Local validation is complete within scope; no full-depth run was made and whole-suite quick coverage is delegated to the hosted PR gate after the broad changed-file attempt exceeded 20 minutes."
  "2026-11-15T06:23:26.427Z",codex-sol,"Hosted run 43684209484 exposed two workflow integration regressions: the direct Node22 test command lost npm test's implicit local-bin PATH, causing pm ENOENT fixtures; fixed by explicitly restoring that PATH. The unchanged release attestation verifier rejects a dynamic matrix executable as unresolved, so deep npm/Bun gates now use separate literal commands selected by matrix conditions. The release verifier itself is untouched, and its command now passes locally. Node22 completed in 11m27s including queue, but that failed run is not acceptance evidence."
  "2026-11-15T06:32:24.290Z",codex-sol,"Retuning after the four-worker covered job exceeded 20 minutes: coverage will use its original two-worker gate, while the uncovered Node22 leg keeps four workers. The temporary worker override and its source/unit changes are fully reverted; no production coverage gate change remains in the final diff. The 25/186 closeout prefix remains. Node22 PATH restoration has an actual-shell positive/negative regression, passing under Node and native Bun. Literal deep commands pass the unchanged release attestation verifier."
  "2026-11-15T06:38:21.347Z",codex-sol,"The superseded covered run's log separates the residual cost: 926.280 seconds in tests, then about 459 seconds aggregating coverage; its final table was 100/100/100/100, with only the known attestation test failure. Import workflow shell scenarios repeat expensive real CLI setup in a generated registration corpus. Quick now registers the same first 25 shell scenarios; full/default registers every original scenario, unchanged. Core import unit tests before that corpus remain in both tiers. This retains every former check in at least one tier and targets expensive exhaustive workflow combinations without changing coverage scope or thresholds."
  "2026-11-15T06:40:09.046Z",codex-sol,"The selected import-workflow registration path passed a real clean-import/publication/second-run scenario locally. Static AST inspection found 33 direct workflow scenario definitions and no nested test registrations, so deferring these definitions preserves their callbacks and parameter-loop closures. All original scenarios remain registered at full/default depth; the exact generated count is logged by the corpus. Preparing hosted validation of the quick prefix with unchanged all-source thresholds."
  "2026-11-15T06:46:55.785Z",codex-sol,"Existing acceptance gap, unchanged by CI v2: two lifecycle-compensation cases are quarantined for the pinned SDK due to pm-cli#1656. The baseline main log and superseded covered trial both show these exact two skips. Existing blocked follow-up pm-github-quay already tracks transaction-owned lifecycle compensation, so no duplicate item is created. Full source coverage must not be presented as proof of those skipped upstream SDK contracts."
  "2026-11-15T06:58:11.886Z",codex-sol,"Run 43686568201 again crossed the 15-minute wall budget with negligible queueing. The remaining serial closeout publication corpus has 49 scenarios: baseline execution 393.834 seconds, versus 174.549 seconds for its first 25. Quick now registers that prefix; deep/default retains all 49 scenarios and all 186 decision cells. A shared test-only collector preserves the exact original callbacks and options for both workflow corpora; unit controls verify default/unknown-depth completeness and quick prefix order. No coverage source, threshold, or production gate implementation is changed."
  "2026-11-15T07:09:04.167Z",codex-sol,"First complete hosted success: run 43686568201 at da98eb62ce06343a58ecd0a8b5bb2094f0e663f4. Jobs API created-to-completed: test (22) 17m27s, test (26) 22m25s; each queued 2s. Node26 passed 2129 tests with zero failures/cancellations and the two unchanged SDK quarantines; all 34 authored modules reached exact 100/100/100/100. Native Bun metadata/lifecycle and bunx smoke passed. This proves functionality but misses the 15-minute target. The measured remaining publication corpus is being reduced to its first 25/49 scenarios in quick mode, with all full/default scenarios retained. Local selected publication replay passed in 38.545s; shared collector controls passed under Node and Bun."
  "2026-11-15T07:14:17.272Z",codex-sol,"Deep-only harness correction: the original native Bun suite command hard-coded a 600000ms per-test limit, which would ignore PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3. The deep workflow now retains the same complete file glob and aggregate failure behavior, restores npm's local CLI PATH, and passes Bun a 1800000ms timeout via the required scale. The 120-minute job cap remains. Strict YAML parsing and bash syntax validation pass; no full-depth local suite was executed."
  "2026-11-15T07:29:11.758Z",codex-sol,"Run 43688644393 at 9d799cf7461d00f7d7d415c171b641cbc5e815ea passed both required checks: test (22) 12m24s, test (26) 15m43s created-to-completed; each queued 2s. Node26: 2106 pass, zero failures/cancellations, two unchanged SDK skips, and exact 100/100/100/100. Covered testing took 699.568s and native aggregation about 203s. With all workflow corpora now bounded, enabling the explicit four-worker quick override to remove the remaining 43-second budget miss; full/default/local-without-override stay at two. The expanded worker and corpus controls pass locally, and native c8 remapping, all-source scope, thresholds and 3GiB merge ceiling remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-15T07:57:43.428Z",codex-sol,"Run 43690285777 passed both required checks, but four-worker coverage regressed to 17m56s (test execution 756.739s plus about 267s aggregation), versus the two-worker 15m43s result. Keeping the original two-worker coverage implementation. The import workflow fixtures now reuse one freshly packed immutable candidate per process, following the existing closeout fixture pattern; every scenario still performs its own real install and uses independent project/tracker state. Explicit clone/worktree packing remains uncached. Local positive, adversarial and clone/worktree packing checks pass with this cache. No production coverage script or coverage thresholds remain changed."
  "2026-11-15T08:38:23.687Z",codex-sol,"Passing cache run 43692426506 at 0e5ae434d13ec1e0db9866d0575411720ca32678: test (22) wall 21m24s = queue 9m15s + execution 12m09s; test (26) wall 25m05s = queue 5m21s + execution 19m44s. Node26 testing took 892.125s and aggregation about 244s; source coverage remained exact 100/100/100/100 with two unchanged SDK quarantines. The current fixture adjustment keeps a unique per-consumer archive locator while sharing only immutable packed bytes. The 15-minute target is not achieved; native aggregation/fixture profiling is tracked separately by pm-github-ci-coverage-latency, and shared-pool queueing remains companion scope. No unsafe coverage filtering or quality relaxation was introduced."
  "2026-11-15T08:42:14.514Z",codex-sol,"The final locator-preserving cache check passed 3/3 real positive/adversarial/clone-worktree scenarios in 278.999s at quick depth and scale 3, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Only packing is shared; each fixture receives its own byte-identical archive at the original locator and performs its own real install into independent state. This keeps package-manager cache identities independent. The separate latency follow-up remains open; main CI v2 acceptance does not claim the 15-minute budget achieved."
  "2026-11-15T08:47:57.643Z",codex-sol,"Handoff receipts: completed source 0e5ae434d13ec1e0db9866d0575411720ca32678 / CI run 43692426506 passed test (22) in 21m24s created-to-completed (9m15s queue, 12m09s execution) and test (26) in 25m05s (5m21s queue, 19m44s execution). Node 26: 2106 pass, zero failures/cancellations, two existing upstream SDK compensation quarantines; all four coverage dimensions 100% across 34 modules. Fastest bounded-corpus run 43688644393 measured 12m24s / 15m43s wall. The 15-minute target remains unmet; pm-github-ci-coverage-latency tracks profiling without native-remapping shortcuts or weakened thresholds. Final locator-preserving source 6283d9aa61f2bb703923c0806953ae7ebe5908e9 passed the focused real positive/adversarial/clone-worktree fixture controls locally (3/3, 278.999s); its PR check receipts will be distinguished by exact head in PR #249. Typecheck, build:test, lint, strict YAML parsing and unchanged release attestation verification passed. Full depth was never executed locally and awaits post-merge deep CI. Strict health driver checks prove current-runner installation only, not developer clone-local state. No release/reusable workflow or verifier modifications; no protection/variable changes; no review-thread interaction; no merge or task closure. Releasing the implementation claim while monitoring final PR checks. Companion pm-cli-website-dyhg."
  "2026-11-15T09:19:23.909Z",codex-sol,"Final workflow/test implementation 9a9a1bbff50d9c1834fa3022ba5080803b9c5b42 passed CI run 43696188386. Jobs API: test (22) created-to-completed 16m43s = queue 5m33s + execution 11m10s; test (26) 29m03s = queue 7m05s + execution 21m58s. Each had 2106 passes, zero failures/cancellations and the two existing SDK compensation skips. Correction: earlier comments saying 34 authored modules were transcription errors; the unchanged native coverage gate reports 32 authored modules with exact 100/100/100/100 in this and the cited earlier green runs. Node26 testing took 1035.706s and aggregation about 233s; all eight native Bun smoke tests and installed bunx launcher passed. CodeQL and Greptile passed. The 15-minute acceptance target remains unmet; packed SDK fixtures and native aggregation dominate execution while hosted queueing remains separately visible. Full-depth deep CI is pending post-merge; no coverage thresholds or source inventory were weakened. This final change only corrects documentation/tracker receipts; workflow/test bytes match the tested implementation. Claim remains released and both tasks remain open. Exact receipt-head CI results are reported separately in PR #249 to avoid confusing metadata changes with source certification."
  "2026-11-15T13:42:38.293Z",codex-sol,"Review round: preserve cheap-path privacy and identity checks where applicable, restore portable test behavior, and verify generated-case assertions. Run targeted gates and required revert proofs; leave review threads untouched and wait for the dispatch hold before pushing."
  "2026-11-15T13:51:28.981Z",codex-sol,"Review findings PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM63pJAn and PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM63pJAp fixed: docs/tracker jobs run the comprehensive privacy gate independently of product tests; the request deadline upper assertion is unscaled while the outer runner watchdog remains scaled. Linked gates passed: typecheck, build, test compilation, lint, 69 HTTP/routing/privacy tests, strict unique-key YAML, changelog and privacy checks. An additional 11 release/changelog tooling tests passed; the deadline-only test passed at scale 3 in 30.057 seconds. Required test (26) run 43698700451 failed solely on stale CHANGELOG.md: release-tag discovery expected an empty Unreleased section. Requested gh run view --log-failed returned empty, so retrieved the job log through the GitHub API; regenerated canonical changelog and verified it. No separate identity/secret scripts exist beyond the comprehensive privacy gate. No measured coverage sources changed; package coverage was not run. Review threads untouched; no CI wait after push."
  "2026-11-15T14:24:10.841Z",codex-sol,"Round 2: fixing the supplied review findings, auditing the whole CI v2 diff for the same defect classes, and running the requested focused gates. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-15T14:34:24.484Z",codex-sol,"Round 2 audit complete: all 30 original testTime calls are listed in docs/ci-tiers.md. Fifteen product assertions and six associated diagnostic calls are now fixed; nine harness calls retain scaling. Validation passed: typecheck, lint, build/build:test; 197 tests at normal scale; 205 tests at scale 3 via pm test --run --only-last --progress; isolated installed-import repeat at both scales (one test each); strict parsing of every workflow. Threads remain untouched."
